faqs:
  - q: "Can you migrate my data from another CRM or spreadsheet?"
    a: "Yes. We handle the entire migration process. Whether you are coming from Salesforce, HubSpot, Jobber, a Google Sheet, or a stack of paper files, we will import your contacts, conversation history, and deal data into GullStack CRM. Most migrations take 3-5 business days, and we verify every record to make sure nothing gets lost."
  - q: "Does the CRM integrate with my other tools?"
    a: "GullStack CRM is built to integrate with the tools you already use. It connects natively with Google Workspace, Outlook, QuickBooks, and most popular business software. For custom integrations, we build API connections that sync data automatically. The biggest advantage is that the CRM is natively integrated with our website, booking, payment, and automation tools — no third-party connectors needed."
  - q: "Can I access the CRM from my phone?"
    a: "Absolutely. The CRM is fully responsive and works on any device — phone, tablet, or desktop. You get real-time notifications when new leads come in, can view customer history on the go, respond to messages, and update deal stages from anywhere. No app download required — it works directly in your mobile browser."
  - q: "How is this different from Salesforce or HubSpot?"
    a: "Salesforce and HubSpot are built for enterprise sales teams with dedicated admins to configure and maintain them. They are powerful, but they are overkill for most small businesses — and they cost $50-300+ per user per month. GullStack CRM is designed for business owners who want to stay organized without becoming software experts. It is simpler, faster to set up, and a fraction of the cost."
  - q: "What if I only have a few customers? Do I really need a CRM?"
    a: "If you have customers, you need a system to track them. Even businesses with 20-30 clients benefit from a CRM because it ensures nothing falls through the cracks — no forgotten follow-ups, no lost contact information, no missed opportunities. The earlier you start tracking customer relationships properly, the easier it is to scale when your business grows."
