<!-- Hero -->
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="section-tag">CRM</span>
    <h1>One Dashboard. Every Customer. <span class="gradient-text">Zero Chaos.</span></h1>
    <p>Every lead, every conversation, every payment, every appointment — in one place. No more sticky notes, scattered spreadsheets, or forgotten follow-ups. A CRM built for how small businesses actually work.</p>
    <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">See It In Action &#8594;</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Problem Section -->
<section class="problem-section">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="section-tag">The Problem</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align:center;">Your Customer Data Lives in 6 Different Places</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">You have leads in your email, phone numbers in your contacts, notes in a spreadsheet, conversations in text messages, and payment records in another app. Nothing talks to anything else, and things fall through the cracks daily.</p>
    <div class="highlight-box fade-in">
      <ul>
        <li>You forgot to follow up with a hot prospect from last week because their info was buried in your inbox</li>
        <li>A customer called and you had no idea what you discussed with them two months ago</li>
        <li>Your "CRM" is a Google Sheet that is always out of date and missing half the information</li>
        <li>You are paying $50-300/month for Salesforce or HubSpot but only use 10% of the features</li>
        <li>New leads from your website go to one place, phone calls to another, and social media messages to a third</li>
        <li>You cannot answer the simple question: "How many active leads do I have right now?"</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Solution Section -->
<section class="solution-section">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="section-tag">The Solution</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align:center;">A CRM That Actually Makes Your Life Easier</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">GullStack CRM is designed for business owners — not enterprise sales teams. It is simple enough to use on day one and powerful enough to grow with your business.</p>
    <div class="solution-copy fade-in">
      <p>Every customer interaction lives in one unified timeline. When someone fills out a form on your website, they appear in your CRM instantly. When they book an appointment, it shows up on their record. When they make a payment, it is tracked automatically. When you text them, the conversation is logged. No manual data entry. No switching between apps.</p>
      <p>The real power is integration. GullStack CRM is not a standalone tool you have to connect to everything else with Zapier and duct tape. It is natively built into the same platform as your website, booking system, payment processing, and marketing automation. Everything just works together.</p>
      <p>The result is a complete picture of every customer relationship — from first contact to latest payment — in a single dashboard that takes five minutes to learn.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

